# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to comit your .python-version file.
#   For an app development deployment, you might want to ignore it.
#.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of microservices or internal apps, you might opt to ignore it.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Poetry uses poetry.lock to ensure reproducible builds. It's recommended to commit it.
#pointer-files
#poetry.lock

